IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wills-dates`
IMPORT `wills-rules`
IMPORT `wills-seat`

-- Wills Act 1997 (Vic) -- worked cases for the will-maker's questions (wills-seat.l4) and the date helpers.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output.
-- Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases: the will-maker`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

§§ `Dates`

-- February 2028 has 29 days (leap year), December 31, April 30; January 2027 runs 30 days from the 1st to the 31st.
#ASSERT `the days in month` 2 `of` 2028 EQUALS 29
#ASSERT `the days in month` 2 `of` 2027 EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `the days in month` 12 `of` 2027 EQUALS 31
#ASSERT `the days in month` 4 `of` 2027 EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 1 1 2027) `to` (`d` 31 1 2027) EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `the date` 30 `days after` (`d` 15 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 16 3 2028
-- Six months from a day: the same day-number six months on, or the last day of a shorter month.
#ASSERT `the last day of` 6 `months from` (`d` 10 1 2027) EQUALS `d` 10 7 2027
#ASSERT `the last day of` 6 `months from` (`d` 15 7 2027) EQUALS `d` 15 1 2028
#ASSERT `the last day of` 6 `months from` (`d` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `the last day of` 6 `months from` (`d` 31 8 2026) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `the last day of` 6 `months from` (`d` 30 12 2027) EQUALS `d` 30 6 2028
#ASSERT `the last day of` 6 `months from` (`d` 31 12 2027) EQUALS `d` 30 6 2028

§§ `ss 5, 6, 20 -- is my will valid as to my age`

-- Arguments: age, marital status, in contemplation of a marriage, Court order under s 20.
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as to my age` 18 `never married` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I am 18 or over`
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as to my age` 18 `never married` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I am 18 or over`
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as to my age` 17 `never married` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a will made by a minor is not valid (s 5)`
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as to my age` 17 `married now` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I am a married minor (s 6(b))`
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as to my age` 17 `never married` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes, but it has no effect if the marriage I contemplate does not take place (s 6(a))`
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as to my age` 17 `never married` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Court authorised it by an order under s 20`
-- A widowed or divorced minor may revoke (s 6(c)) but not make a new will (finding 1).
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as to my age` 16 `married before, but not now (divorced or widowed)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a will made by a minor is not valid (s 5)`
#ASSERT `Is my will valid as to my age` 17 `married before, but not now (divorced or widowed)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes, but it has no effect if the marriage I contemplate does not take place (s 6(a))`

§§ `ss 6, 20 -- can I revoke my will as a minor`

-- Arguments: age, marital status, made in contemplation of marriage, made while married, Court order.
#ASSERT `Can I revoke my will as a minor` 18 `never married` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I revoke my will as a minor` 17 `never married` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I revoke my will as a minor` 17 `married now` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I revoke my will as a minor` 17 `never married` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I revoke my will as a minor` 17 `married before, but not now (divorced or widowed)` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I revoke my will as a minor` 17 `married before, but not now (divorced or widowed)` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I revoke my will as a minor` 17 `never married` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 20 -- can the Court authorise my will as a minor`

-- Arguments: age, understands, reflects intentions, reasonable.
#ASSERT `Can the Court authorise my will as a minor` 17 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court authorise my will as a minor` 17 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court authorise my will as a minor` 17 TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court authorise my will as a minor` 17 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court authorise my will as a minor` 18 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 7, 10 -- signed and witnessed in person`

-- Arguments: in writing, who signed, intending a will, witnesses present together, of them how many signed in my presence.
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed in person` TRUE `I signed it myself` TRUE 2 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed in person` TRUE `someone else signed it, in my presence and at my direction` TRUE 2 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed in person` TRUE `someone else signed it, but not in my presence or not at my direction` TRUE 2 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed in person` TRUE `nobody signed it` TRUE 2 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed in person` FALSE `I signed it myself` TRUE 2 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed in person` TRUE `I signed it myself` FALSE 2 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed in person` TRUE `I signed it myself` TRUE 1 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed in person` TRUE `I signed it myself` TRUE 2 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed in person` TRUE `I signed it myself` TRUE 3 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed in person` TRUE `I signed it myself` TRUE 3 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Only one witness was present when I signed; a second signed later: s 7(1)(c) fails.
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed in person` TRUE `I signed it myself` TRUE 1 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 7(5), 8A, 19E(2) -- signed and witnessed remotely`

-- Arguments: international will, special witness, number of witnesses, same day in Victoria, all saw, special witness last,
-- link witnesses' statements and signatures, special witness's check and statement.
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed remotely` FALSE `an Australian legal practitioner` 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed remotely` FALSE `a justice of the peace` 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed remotely` FALSE `a member of a prescribed class` 3 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed remotely` FALSE `no special witness` 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed remotely` TRUE `an Australian legal practitioner` 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed remotely` FALSE `an Australian legal practitioner` 1 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed remotely` FALSE `an Australian legal practitioner` 2 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed remotely` FALSE `an Australian legal practitioner` 2 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed remotely` FALSE `an Australian legal practitioner` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed remotely` FALSE `an Australian legal practitioner` 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my will validly signed and witnessed remotely` FALSE `an Australian legal practitioner` 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 11 -- a witness who benefits`

#ASSERT `Can a witness who benefits keep the gift` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can a witness who benefits keep the gift` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 17 -- a will made under another law`

-- Arguments: law of the place executed, of domicile or habitual residence, of nationality, for land the law where it is.
#ASSERT `Is my will made abroad properly executed` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will made abroad properly executed` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will made abroad properly executed` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will made abroad properly executed` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my will made abroad properly executed` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 15 -- is my change effective`

-- Arguments: made after execution, signed and witnessed, original words no longer apparent.
#ASSERT `Is my change to my will effective` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my change to my will effective` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my change to my will effective` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my change to my will effective` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my change to my will effective` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my change to my will effective` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 49A -- the charging clause`

-- Arguments: day the will was executed, written informed consent, given before execution. s 49A commenced 1 November 2017.
#ASSERT `Is the charging clause in my will valid` (`d` 1 11 2017) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the charging clause in my will valid` (`d` 1 11 2017) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the charging clause in my will valid` (`d` 31 10 2017) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the charging clause in my will valid` (`d` 15 3 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the charging clause in my will valid` (`d` 15 3 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the charging clause in my will valid` (`d` 15 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 12 -- have I revoked my will`

-- Arguments: how, executed as a will, later will revokes it, who did it, intending to revoke, Court satisfied from its state.
#ASSERT `Have I revoked my will` `by a later will` TRUE TRUE `I did` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Have I revoked my will` `by a later will` TRUE FALSE `I did` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Have I revoked my will` `by a later will` FALSE TRUE `I did` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Have I revoked my will` `by a writing declaring that I revoke it` TRUE FALSE `I did` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Have I revoked my will` `by a writing declaring that I revoke it` FALSE FALSE `I did` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Have I revoked my will` `by burning, tearing or otherwise destroying it` FALSE FALSE `I did` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Have I revoked my will` `by burning, tearing or otherwise destroying it` FALSE FALSE `someone else, in my presence and at my direction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Have I revoked my will` `by burning, tearing or otherwise destroying it` FALSE FALSE `someone else, not in my presence or not at my direction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Have I revoked my will` `by burning, tearing or otherwise destroying it` FALSE FALSE `I did` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Have I revoked my will` `by writing on it or otherwise dealing with it` FALSE FALSE `I did` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Have I revoked my will` `by writing on it or otherwise dealing with it` FALSE FALSE `I did` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Have I revoked my will` `by writing on it or otherwise dealing with it` FALSE FALSE `someone else, not in my presence or not at my direction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Have I revoked my will` `in some other way (telling someone, or a writing not signed and witnessed)` TRUE TRUE `I did` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 12, 13 -- marriage and new relationships`

-- Arguments: the new relationship, made in contemplation of this marriage, expressed in contemplation of marriage generally.
#ASSERT `Does my marriage revoke my will` `none` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nothing: there has been no marriage since the will was made`
#ASSERT `Does my marriage revoke my will` `I began a domestic relationship (registered, or living together as a couple) without marrying` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nothing: only a marriage revokes a will, not a domestic relationship (ss 12, 13)`
#ASSERT `Does my marriage revoke my will` `I married` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `nothing: the will was made in contemplation of this marriage (s 13(3)(a))`
#ASSERT `Does my marriage revoke my will` `I married` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `nothing: the will is expressed to be made in contemplation of marriage generally (s 13(3)(b))`
#ASSERT `Does my marriage revoke my will` `I married` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `nothing: the will was made in contemplation of this marriage (s 13(3)(a))`
#ASSERT `Does my marriage revoke my will` `I married` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the will is revoked, except gifts to and appointments of the person I am married to at my death, and the powers s 13(2)(c) saves`

§§ `ss 12, 14 -- divorce`

-- Arguments: how it ended, will existed at the divorce, the part, it appears I wanted it kept.
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `a divorce under the Family Law Act 1975 took effect` TRUE `a gift to my former spouse` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `the Family Court annulled the marriage` TRUE `my former spouse as executor` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `the marriage was dissolved or annulled overseas, in a way recognised in Australia` TRUE `my former spouse as trustee` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `a divorce under the Family Law Act 1975 took effect` TRUE `my former spouse as advisory trustee or guardian` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `a divorce under the Family Law Act 1975 took effect` TRUE `a power of appointment exercisable by or in favour of my former spouse` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `a divorce under the Family Law Act 1975 took effect` TRUE `my former spouse as trustee of property left on trust for beneficiaries who include their children` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `a divorce under the Family Law Act 1975 took effect` TRUE `a power of appointment exercisable by my former spouse only in favour of our children` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `we separated, but there is no divorce or annulment` TRUE `a gift to my former spouse` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `a domestic relationship (not a marriage) ended` TRUE `a gift to my former spouse` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `a divorce under the Family Law Act 1975 took effect` FALSE `a gift to my former spouse` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my divorce revoke this part of my will` `a divorce under the Family Law Act 1975 took effect` TRUE `a gift to my former spouse` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 16 -- revival`

-- Arguments: re-executed, codicil showing intention to revive, partly then wholly revoked, contrary intention.
#ASSERT `Is my revoked will revived` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the will is revived (s 16(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my revoked will revived` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the will is revived (s 16(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my revoked will revived` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not revive it on these facts`
#ASSERT `Is my revoked will revived` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not revive it on these facts`
#ASSERT `Is my revoked will revived` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `only the part most recently revoked is revived (s 16(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my revoked will revived` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the will is revived (s 16(1))`

§§ `s 24 -- a Court-authorised will`

#ASSERT `Can I change my Court-authorised will myself` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I change my Court-authorised will myself` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
